   "geometry_speed": false,
   "_note": "STEADY (matthew930am, 2026-11-07): untuned, conservative course profile. Every value is a choice from recorded evidence, not a fit. Straight legs only (planner waypoints, no navigator arcs): runs 006-010 measured PX4 cross-track p95 0.036-0.069 m on straight non-yawing motion at <= 0.16 m/s, but 0.10-0.15 m on curving paths and 0.06-0.26 m while yawing during translation, and ~0.19 m on straight legs above 0.16 m/s (run004). Hence speed 0.15, blend_turn_deg 0 (every vertex: stop, settle below 0.05 m/s for 0.5 s, turn in place, depth-check, go), heading fixed while moving (pose mode updates yaw only when blending). PX4's velocity estimate departs from truth for ~2 s during every ~50 deg yaw-while-moving sweep (runs 004-010; EV velocity is not fused, EKF2_EV_CTRL 9, so not a frame bug): yawing only while stopped avoids it. tube_gate: forward motion holds while the aircraft is more than the leg's tube_m (planner.leg_tube_m = half the leg's physical slack) across the leg. accel/brake 0.5 m/s^2 (was 0.3; 3-minute rule): braking from the 0.30 m/s cap takes 0.09 m, inside capture_m 0.10. Arrival settle 0.3 s below 0.08 m/s (was 0.5 s / 0.05).",
   "face_tol_deg": 8.0,
   "turn_settle_s": 0.0,
   "_settle_note": "Set-off drift (first 2.5 s of a leg, across it) median ~0.07 m in run013 (face_tol 8, no settle) and in run015 (face_tol 3 + 2 s settle): neither the tighter heading tolerance nor the settle changed it, so both are back to the flown run013 values (face_tol_deg 8, turn_settle_s 0).",
   "yaw_rate_dps": 35.0,
   "tube_response_s": 0.44,
   "leg_speed_cap_mps": 0.4,
   "_speed_note": "RULE 7.9: a run ends at the 3-minute limit (clock from leaving the launch mark, rule 7.5). run015 took ~287 s. Per-leg cruise = planner.leg_speed_mps(tube_m, tube_response_s, leg_speed_cap_mps): tube / 0.44 s, where 0.44 s is run015's measured p90 of (steady cross-track p95 / speed) per leg; cap 0.40 m/s: run016 flew the open legs at 0.25-0.30 m/s with steady cross-track p95/speed 0.11-0.33 s (<= the 0.44 s basis), so the linear relation held there; 0.40 extrapolates it by 1/3. Maze/window legs ~0.15-0.20 m/s, tunnel/chicane ~0.30. speed_mps 0.15 remains the default for legs without a tube. yaw_rate_dps stays at the flown 35: in-place turns slide the body 5-8 cm (runs 013/015, real motion PX4 sees) and vertex clearances are 0.46-0.53 m; a higher rate is unmeasured. hold_s 0.25 (arrival already requires settling).",
   "excite_yaw_deg": 0.0,
   "excite_settle_s": 2.0,
   "_excite_note": "OFF. run017 (b783000) flew excite_yaw 90 at the take-off point: the camera faced the west net at 0.50 m (92 % open, depth sees through it to unmapped space; OAK minimum range 0.4 m) and the estimate failed: the body slid 0.357 m, PX4 local position moved ~1.4 m, xy_valid went false 5.2 s into the yaw and refnav landed (Program FAILED, 7.2 s airborne). From the take-off point every heading except the start one faces a surface at 0.50-0.55 m, which breaks leg_policy face_min_m 0.8 (the rule every in-place turn on the route obeys). A first-yaw excitation needs a place whose whole yaw arc keeps that facing distance; there is none at this start, so it stays off.",
   "first_turn_gate_s": 4.5,
   "_first_turn_note": "first_turn_gate_s 4.5: after the first >= 20 deg in-place turn only, go once |PX4 - setpoint| < 0.03 m and speed < 0.02 m/s (timeout 4.5 s: run014's 60 deg turn recovered to < 0.03 m at +4.3 s). PX4's post-yaw velocity error: first yaw 0.085 (run015) / 0.091 (run016) m/s, later yaws <= 0.021 / 0.033. Leg 2 (after that turn) was every steady run's minimum leg (0.299, 0.299, 0.277 m) and in run016 spent 6.5 of its 8.1 s creeping on tube holds after a 0.173 m set-off drift.",
   "yaw_accel_dps2": 0.0,
   "_yaw_profile_note": "Before: the turn slewed the yaw setpoint at a constant 35 deg/s from the first tick to the last (yaw acceleration steps) while publishing trajectory_setpoint.yawspeed 0.0 (the message default; run021 published_trajectory), so PX4 followed on feedback alone: ~1.35 s of heading lag per turn (run016). yaw_accel_dps2 90: trapezoidal yaw-rate profile with the rate published as yawspeed feed-forward. 90 deg/s^2 = 35 deg/s over ~one yaw time constant of PX4's default attitude loop (MC_YAW_P 2.8 -> 0.36 s), so the loop can follow the ramp. Whether the abrupt profile drove part of the 5-20 cm in-place slide is the next run's question; the profile is standard multirotor practice either way.",
   "arrive_tight_m": 0.0,
   "arrive_tight_mps": 0.03,
   "arrive_timeout_s": 3.0,
   "_arrival_note": "run021 turn diagnosis (bag + truth): the in-place turn started while the aircraft was still arriving, 3.6 cm short and 3.5 cm/s median (13 cm / 7.8 cm/s worst) under the loose test (0.15 m, < 0.08 m/s for 0.3 s); the arrival ran on through the turn and overshot by up to 11 cm: the post-turn reversal. Stops without a turn moved 5-7 cm vs 9-10 cm with one, so yaw adds ~3-4 cm; VIO stayed within 2 cm of truth through every turn. The reversal comes from the tail of that distribution: median handoffs (3.6 cm, 3.5 cm/s) overshot ~1.4 cm, the worst (13 cm / 7.8 cm/s) 8-11 cm. arrive_tight_m 0.05 / arrive_tight_mps 0.03 for arrive_settle_s cuts the tail; 0.03 / 0.02 cost +33 s offline (timeouts) for the median cases; arrive_timeout_s 3.0 after capture falls back to the loose test (PX4's position loop closes with tau ~1.05 s, so ~3 tau reaches the tight bound from the 0.10 m capture). OFF for now (arrive_tight_m 0): in run021/run016 PX4's hold reached 5 cm / 3 cm/s for 0.3 s within 10 s at only 10/20 and 6/20 stops (p50 0.4-0.6 s when it did, p90 1.6-2.5 s), so the gate would often wait for its timeout: +15-30 s per run against the 180 s limit (run021 183.3 s). Enable when the yawspeed feed-forward has bought the time."
